    "body": "Maybe because this new methods (prepend/append/before/after/replaceWith) operate on multiple arguments and using fragment is easiest to modify the tree in the next steps. All of them [using convert nodes into a node](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#converting-nodes-into-a-node) and for multiple nodes can leake this #document-fragment as parent (when conversion faild like above example).\r\n\r\nBut fragment as transient node also enters additional restrictions:\r\n`document.append(dtd)` << work because we not use fragment (pass one argument)\r\n `document.append(comment, dtd)` << faild because we can't put dtd to fragment via [ensure pre-insertion validity](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-ensure-pre-insertion-validity) but for the document itself it's correct.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
